  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[{t}^{2}(2t+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}+8t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =6(2)^{2}+8(2) \\\\  & =24+16 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$",
